%% title: Budget thresholds and where their alerts go
%% alt: The budget lab-az104-04-cost-monthly, 5 a month on rg-lab-az104-04-cost from the 1st, has three thresholds: 50% and 80% of actual spend and 100% of forecast spend. Each one alerts the action group lab-az104-04-cost-budget-alerts, which has no receivers yet, so nothing is sent until you add one.
flowchart TB
  rg("rg-lab-az104-04-cost<br/>spend")
  b{{"budget lab-az104-04-cost-monthly<br/>5 a month, from the 1st"}}
  t1{{"50% of actual"}}
  t2{{"80% of actual"}}
  t3{{"100% of forecast"}}
  ag("action group<br/>lab-az104-04-cost-budget-alerts<br/>short name labbudget")
  nr(["no receivers yet:<br/>nothing is emailed or called"])
  rg -. "measured by" .-> b
  b --> t1 & t2 & t3
  t1 & t2 & t3 --> ag
  ag -.-> nr
  class rg,ag azure
  class b,t1,t2,t3 rule
  class nr client
  classDef azure fill:#eaf0fa,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f1b2d
  classDef client fill:#f4f7fb,stroke:#768498,color:#0f1b2d
  classDef rule fill:#fff7e6,stroke:#b45309,color:#0f1b2d
